{{ 'ness-hero.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

{%- liquid
  assign heading_id = 'ness-hero-heading-' | append: section.id
  assign cine_id = 'ness-hero-cine-' | append: section.id
  comment
    Always three: each layer now falls back to a bundled photograph, so a
    merchant cannot reduce the count by clearing an image. The CSS keys its
    delays off this, and three is what the design's -8s spacing is built for.
  endcomment
  assign layer_count = 3
-%}

<section
  class="ness-hero"
  {% if section.settings.heading != blank %}aria-labelledby="{{ heading_id }}"{% endif %}
>
  {%- comment -%}
    The photographs are decorative — the headline beside them carries the
    meaning — so alt is empty and the layer is hidden from assistive tech.
    The first is eager and fetchpriority high because it is the largest
    contentful paint on the page; the others are eager (they are on screen
    within seconds) but left at default priority so they do not compete with
    it.

    Slots two and three have no bundled fallback on purpose: an unchosen slot
    renders no layer at all rather than a placeholder, and data-cine-count
    tells the stylesheet how many there are to cross-fade between. One
    photograph gets no animation — see ness-hero.css.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="ness-hero__media" data-cine-count="{{ layer_count }}" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="ness-hero__layer">
      {%- if section.settings.image != blank -%}
        {{
          section.settings.image
          | image_url: width: 2400
          | image_tag:
            alt: '',
            widths: '750, 1100, 1500, 1900, 2400',
            sizes: '100vw',
            loading: 'eager',
            fetchpriority: 'high'
        }}
      {%- else -%}
        <img
          src="{{ 'ness-hero-bg.jpg' | asset_url }}"
          alt=""
          width="1000"
          height="667"
          loading="eager"
          fetchpriority="high"
        >
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    <div class="ness-hero__layer">
      {%- if section.settings.image_2 != blank -%}
        {{
          section.settings.image_2
          | image_url: width: 2400
          | image_tag:
            alt: '',
            widths: '750, 1100, 1500, 1900, 2400',
            sizes: '100vw',
            loading: 'eager',
            fetchpriority: 'low'
        }}
      {%- else -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Bundled so the crossfade the design specifies actually happens on a
          fresh install. Without a default here layer_count fell to 1, the hero
          degraded to a single still, and the pause control never rendered
          because there was nothing to pause.

          fetchpriority low: all three layers are viewport-sized and in view, so
          lazy would not defer them either, and without this they compete with
          layer one — the LCP candidate and the only one visible at t=0.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <img
          src="{{ 'ness-hero-bg-2.jpg' | asset_url }}"
          alt=""
          width="1000"
          height="659"
          loading="eager"
          fetchpriority="low"
        >
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    <div class="ness-hero__layer">
      {%- if section.settings.image_3 != blank -%}
        {{
          section.settings.image_3
          | image_url: width: 2400
          | image_tag:
            alt: '',
            widths: '750, 1100, 1500, 1900, 2400',
            sizes: '100vw',
            loading: 'eager',
            fetchpriority: 'low'
        }}
      {%- else -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Bundled so the crossfade the design specifies actually happens on a
          fresh install. Without a default here layer_count fell to 1, the hero
          degraded to a single still, and the pause control never rendered
          because there was nothing to pause.

          fetchpriority low: all three layers are viewport-sized and in view, so
          lazy would not defer them either, and without this they compete with
          layer one — the LCP candidate and the only one visible at t=0.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <img
          src="{{ 'ness-hero-bg-3.jpg' | asset_url }}"
          alt=""
          width="667"
          height="1000"
          loading="eager"
          fetchpriority="low"
        >
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="ness-hero__wash" aria-hidden="true"></div>

  {%- comment -%}
    Play/pause for the crossfade. Rendered only when there is more than one
    photograph, because with one there is no animation to hold.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if layer_count > 1 -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      A checkbox, not a button, and no JavaScript.

      WCAG 2.2.2 requires a pause control for anything that moves for more than
      five seconds, and this loop is infinite. A scripted button fails that the
      moment JavaScript is blocked — the CSS keeps animating and the control
      never appears. `:checked ~` pauses a CSS animation with no script at all,
      so the guarantee holds unconditionally.

      role="switch" gives it the right semantics: the accessible name stays
      "Pause the slideshow" and aria-checked carries the state, rather than a
      changing name plus aria-pressed, which announces "Play, pressed" — the
      exact inverse of what is true.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <input
      type="checkbox"
      id="{{ cine_id }}"
      class="ness-hero__cine-input"
      role="switch"
    >
    <label class="ness-hero__cine" for="{{ cine_id }}">
      <svg class="ness-hero__cine-icon ness-hero__cine-icon--pause" width="12" height="14" viewBox="0 0 12 14" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
        <rect x="0" y="0" width="4" height="14" rx="1"/>
        <rect x="8" y="0" width="4" height="14" rx="1"/>
      </svg>
      <svg class="ness-hero__cine-icon ness-hero__cine-icon--play" width="12" height="14" viewBox="0 0 12 14" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
        <path d="M0 0.8 C0 0.1 0.8 -0.3 1.4 0.1 L11.4 6.3 C11.9 6.6 11.9 7.4 11.4 7.7 L1.4 13.9 C0.8 14.3 0 13.9 0 13.2 Z"/>
      </svg>
      <span class="ness-hero__cine-label ness-hero__cine-label--pause">Pause</span>
      <span class="ness-hero__cine-label ness-hero__cine-label--play">Play</span>
      <span class="visually-hidden"> the slideshow</span>
    </label>
  {%- endif -%}

  <div class="ness-hero__content">
    {%- if section.settings.heading != blank -%}
      <h1 class="ness-hero__heading" id="{{ heading_id }}">
        {{- section.settings.heading | escape -}}
      </h1>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- if section.settings.body != blank -%}
      <p class="ness-hero__body">{{ section.settings.body | escape }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment -%}
      Quick links into the page below. data-smooth is picked up by
      ness-motion.js; without it these remain ordinary anchors that jump, so
      the panel works with scripting disabled.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- assign links = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'link' -%}
    {%- if links.size > 0 -%}
      <nav class="ness-hero__links" aria-label="Jump to section">
        {%- for block in links -%}
          <a
            class="ness-hero__link"
            href="#{{ block.settings.target }}"
            data-smooth
            {{ block.shopify_attributes }}
          >
            <span>{{ block.settings.label | escape }}</span>
            <svg width="13" height="9" viewBox="0 0 12.126 8.907" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
              <path d="M 12.126 1.241 L 11.144 0 L 6.063 6.416 L 0.982 0 L 0 1.241 L 6.063 8.907 L 12.126 1.241 Z"/>
            </svg>
          </a>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </nav>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>
</section>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Hero",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Full-height opening photographs with the headline over them. Add two or three and they cross-fade on a slow loop with a play/pause control; add one and it sits still. Type, colours, and the dark overlay are fixed by the design."
    },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "image",
      "label": "Background photograph 1",
      "info": "Fills the screen and is cropped to fit, so nothing stretches. Use a wide landscape image of at least 2400px. Keep the subject away from the top-left, where the headline sits. Left empty, the photograph the theme ships with is used."
    },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "image_2",
      "label": "Background photograph 2",
      "info": "Optional. Same guidance as the first. Left empty, the hero simply shows fewer photographs — nothing is left blank."
    },
    {
      "type": "image_picker",
      "id": "image_3",
      "label": "Background photograph 3",
      "info": "Optional. Three photographs is what the loop was drawn for and gives the smoothest result."
    },
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Headline", "default": "Nessclusive, Be Bold, Be Exclusive", "info": "Around 30 characters is what the design was drawn for." },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "body", "label": "Sub-heading", "default": "Let your Wig do the talking with Nessclusive" }
  ],
  "max_blocks": 3,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "link",
      "name": "Quick link",
      "settings": [
        { "type": "text", "id": "label", "label": "Wording", "default": "Our Service" },
        {
          "type": "select",
          "id": "target",
          "label": "Scrolls to",
          "default": "services",
          "info": "Sections further down this page. The page scrolls smoothly to whichever you pick.",
          "options": [
            { "value": "services", "label": "Services" },
            { "value": "book", "label": "Book a session" },
            { "value": "about", "label": "About us" },
            { "value": "luxury", "label": "Luxury Looks" },
            { "value": "collections", "label": "Explore Collection" },
            { "value": "faq", "label": "FAQ" },
            { "value": "contact", "label": "Contact" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "default": {
    "blocks": [
      { "type": "link", "settings": { "label": "Our Service", "target": "services" } },
      { "type": "link", "settings": { "label": "Luxury Looks", "target": "luxury" } },
      { "type": "link", "settings": { "label": "Booking", "target": "book" } }
    ]
  }
}
{% endschema %}
